 "reading": "47 of the 78 environment variables the published launchers forward have no reader anywhere in R276's site-packages. That does not mean the behaviour they name is off: a patch series may have made it unconditional at build time. It means the variable no longer controls it, so a recorded container environment showing one of these substantially overstates what is being configured.",
 "why_it_matters": "Three experiments this session were run and written up before it was noticed that the knob under test never reached the container. This is the same failure one level further out: a knob that reaches the container and is read by nothing. Both produce a clean null indistinguishable from a real no-effect result. The campaign harness now asserts a requested knob is present in the container; this audit is how to check the other half, that something reads it.",
